# Svelte 5 UI (`ui/`)

The plugin editor is Svelte **5 runes mode** (Vite + Tailwind). Match existing components in `ui/src/`.

## Required patterns

- **`$props()`** — destructured props with JSDoc `@typedef` (JavaScript project, not TypeScript).
- **`$state()`** — local UI state (dragging, open panels).
- **`$derived` / `$derived.by`** — anything computed from props or state. Do not use `$:`.
- **Events** — `onclick`, `onpointerdown`, etc. Not `on:click`.
- **Composition** — `{#snippet}` + `{@render}`; optional snippet props on children (see `StepCardFlip.svelte`). Callback props (`onValueChange`, `onFlipChange`), not `createEventDispatcher`.
- **Collections** — `SvelteSet` / `SvelteMap` from `svelte/reactivity` when mutating in place (e.g. selection, flip overrides). Reassign `$state` only when replacing the whole collection.
- **Lists** — keyed `{#each}` with stable ids (step IDs), not array indices.

## Avoid (legacy Svelte 4)

`export let`, `$:`, `<slot>` / `$$slots`, `on:event`, stores for local component state, `svelte:component` (use dynamic components), unnecessary `$effect`.

Prefer event handlers or `$derived` over `$effect`. Use `$effect` only when integrating non-Svelte APIs with no cleaner option.

## Before marking UI work done

1. `cd ui && npm run check` — must pass (`--fail-on-warnings`).
2. `cmake --build Builds` — embed fresh `assets/webview/ui.zip` in all plugin binaries (see `rebuild-after-changes.mdc`).

Commits that stage `ui/` run `npm run check` via `.githooks/pre-commit` when hooks are enabled (`./scripts/setup-git-hooks.sh`).

## Scheduling

`phraseSchedule.js` drives the piano-roll preview; C++ owns audio scheduling. Do not change timing in one layer without tests or explicit parity with the other.

## Bridge

Native calls use `@juce` helpers. Keep per-frame native return values small (scalars); avoid large nested payloads on animation paths (see `CLAUDE.md` processor / WebView notes).
